sequenceDiagram
    participant Team as CubeSat team
    participant CSA as Canadian Space Agency
    participant Mission as Canadian Permanent Mission<br/>to the United Nations
    participant UN as UN register (UNOOSA)

    Team->>CSA: Contact the space object registration focal point<br/>with the mission summary and separable spacecraft architecture
    CSA-->>Team: Confirm required information and registration treatment<br/>of the mother and daughter
    Team->>Team: Prepare draft object identification, ownership and general function data

    Note over Team,CSA: Once CSA arranges a launch opportunity
    CSA->>CSA: Obtain launch details through the contracted launch provider<br/>CSA remains the team's launch provider liaison
    CSA-->>Team: Share planned launch date, location and expected orbit
    CSA->>CSA: Coordinate the State of registry with other launching States as applicable
    CSA-->>Team: Confirm registration arrangements for the mission
    Team->>CSA: Update the draft registration information as requested

    Note over Team,UN: After launch and deployment
    Team->>CSA: Provide confirmed launch date and location, object designator and general function<br/>Provide nodal period, inclination, apogee and perigee<br/>for each object identified in the agreed registration approach
    CSA->>CSA: Complete the Canadian national registry entry<br/>including the launching State or States
    CSA->>Mission: Provide registration information for formal UN submission
    Mission->>UN: Submit Canada's registration information<br/>as soon as practicable after launch
    UN->>UN: Record the information in the UN Register and make it publicly accessible
    Team->>Team: Retain the published registration reference in the mission records

    Team->>CSA: Provide updated information or report confirmed end of Earth orbit
    CSA->>CSA: Update the national registry as appropriate
    CSA->>Mission: Provide information for an update to the UN record
    Mission->>UN: Submit the update or end-of-orbit notification
